# A method that does something before it returns a merge. wrap declares a
# field of its own, counts in a loop, changes its formal, and then returns
# merge(add; y: k): the node is built once, where the body ends, with the
# value k has there. wrap 5 binds 8 and wrap 200 binds 0. add reads other,
# a field of the unit, 9: from the root 8 + 1 + 9 and 0 + 1 + 9. under has
# other 20: 29. A second call of the first node gives its own value: 19.
# The merge is written with the model first and the node is called with its
# bound formal left at its default: a bounded case, not the whole of a
# callable merge (steps/defects.md, MERGE-KEEPS-MODEL-INTERFACE). Entry 7.
int: other 9

fn: add (int: y; int: x) int
    return: y + x + other

fn: wrap (int: k) fn: (int: x) int
    int: n 0
    while: n < 3
        k: k + 1
        n: n + 1
    ---
    if: k > 100
        k: 0
    return: merge(add; y: k)

w: wrap 5
u: wrap 200

fn: under () int
    int: other 20
    return: (w: 1)
end: under

int: a (w: 1)
int: b (u: 1)
int: c under()
int: d (w: 2)
int: ok 7
if: a != 18 || b != 10 || c != 29 || d != 19
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
